  "investigation_notes": "Uploads are still failing - app is `unhealthy`, root cause **not proven - `insufficient_evidence`**.\n\n**What was seen:**\n\n- `incidentlab-app-1` is `running` `Up 5 seconds` and `incidentlab-db-1` is `running` `Up 10 seconds (healthy)` [E1].\n- Application `/health` returns `503 {\"status\":\"unhealthy\"}` [E2]. This is a symptom, not a root cause.\n- App container detail: `running:true`, `exit_code:0`, `oom_killed:false`, `restart_count:0`, user `1000:1000`, mount `bind source:/srv/lab-data destination:/data rw:true`, networks `incidentlab_default` [E4].\n- DB container detail: `running:true`, `exit_code:0`, `oom_killed:false`, `health:healthy`, user `(not set: runs as root)`, mount `volume incidentlab_dbdata -> /var/lib/postgresql/data rw:true` [E5].\n- Recent Docker events show orderly `stop/die exit 0/destroy/rename/start` recreates for both containers at `15:56:01` and `15:56:32`, plus `db health_status: healthy` and repeated `pg_isready ... exec_die exit 0` [E6]. No crash / OOM-kill / non-zero exit in this window.\n- Upload directory `/srv/lab-data/uploads` is `is_dir:true`, `owner 1000:1000`, `mode 0755`, `app_uid/app_gid 1000/1000`, `app_user_can_write:true` [E8].\n\n**What this rules out with evidence:**\n- App container down / OOM-killed - ruled out by [E1][E4].\n- DB container down / unhealthy - ruled out by [E1][E5][E6].\n- Missing bind-mount for `/srv/lab-data` - ruled out by [E4].\n- Basic owner/mode permission on uploads preventing write - ruled out by [E8]. Note method is `owner and mode bits only; ignores ACLs` [E8], so ACL / supplementary-group denial not ruled out.\n\n**What is missing - why no diagnosis:**\n- App logs unavailable: `this data source is unavailable` [E3][E11].\n- DB logs unavailable: `this data source is unavailable` [E9].\n- Filesystem capacity/inode for `/srv/lab-data` and `/` unavailable: `this data source is unavailable` [E7][E10][E12].\n\nWithout logs and disk usage, disk-full, inode-full, DB-error-as-root-cause-for-app-503, app-code error, and ACL-based write denial cannot be ruled in or out. Per rule to not conclude a cause only by elimination, outcome is `insufficient_evidence`.\n\n**Needed next, after approval / when sources recover:**\n1. Retry `container_logs incidentlab-app-1` and `incidentlab-db-1` to separate app error vs dependency error.\n2. Retry `disk_usage /srv/lab-data` and `/` for capacity + inodes.\n3. Check effective write e.g. ACLs and test upload, and re-check `app_health`.\n",
